# ============================================================================
#  .gitignore — what does NOT belong in the published repository.
#
#  Two rules of thumb behind every entry below:
#    1. Anything a build produces is excluded. It is regenerated by the build
#       scripts in seconds and, unlike source, it goes stale silently.
#    2. Anything pulled OFF a device is excluded unless the build or the docs
#       actually need it. Device dumps are enormous (the two Gen 6 dumps are
#       1.3 GB each) and they are evidence, not source.
#
#  A trailing slash means "this directory and everything under it", which is
#  the concise way to drop a whole build tree.
#
#  NOTE: .gitignore only affects UNTRACKED files. Anything already added with
#  `git add` keeps being tracked regardless of what is written here — see the
#  `git rm -r --cached` note at the bottom.
# ============================================================================

# ---- bare-metal port: build output -----------------------------------------
# build-owf-image*.sh writes here (owf.elf/.bin, the LVGL archive, every .o);
# tools/mk-bootimg*.sh writes the packed boot images. All reproducible.
fossil-port/baremetal/build/
fossil-port/build/
*.img
*.elf
*.bin
*.o
*.a

# ---- bare-metal port: device dumps -----------------------------------------
# Multi-GB /proc, /sys and device-tree captures from real watches. Kept locally
# as the evidence behind the board headers, far too large to publish.
#
# EXCEPTIONS, unignored below: the C2's compiled device tree is a BUILD INPUT
# (tools/mk-bootimg-c2.sh appends skipjack.dtb by default) and its .dts is what
# boards/ticwatch_c2.h cites line by line, so both must be in the repo.
# `dumps/*` and NOT `dumps/`: git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so
# a trailing-slash exclude cannot be undone by a later `!` on something inside
# it. Excluding the directory's CONTENTS instead leaves the negation working.
fossil-port/dumps/*
!fossil-port/dumps/c2-skipjack-fromsource/

# (The .dtb build inputs at fossil-port/ root — firefish-stock.dtb,
# sda429-hoki.dtb — are not matched by anything above and stay tracked.)

# ---- vendor SDKs and reference trees ---------------------------------------
# Upstream trees kept locally for reference. They are someone else's source,
# they are tens of GB together, and they are all obtainable from their own
# upstreams — nothing here is authored by this project.
tuya_open/
maixcam-port/
Tuya-waveshare-provided-T5-E1/
ESP32-waveshare-provided-*/
ESP32-lilygo-provided-*/

# ---- Arduino / ESP-IDF build output ----------------------------------------
build/
.pio/
.pioenvs/
sdkconfig.old
*.uf2
*.map
*.su

# ---- editor / tooling / OS noise -------------------------------------------
.aider*
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- local scratch ----------------------------------------------------------
*.log
scratch/
tmp/
